#: ../../source/best-practices_client-certificate.md:1
msgid "Client certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_client-certificate.md:3
msgid ""
"Client certificate authentication can be configured with the `Client`, "
"the required options are passed along through the `connect` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_client-certificate.md:5
msgid ""
"The client certificates must be signed by a trusted CA. The Node.js "
"default is to trust the well-known CAs curated by Mozilla."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_client-certificate.md:7
msgid ""
"Setting the server option `requestCert: true` tells the server to request"
" the client certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_client-certificate.md:9
msgid ""
"The server option `rejectUnauthorized: false` allows us to handle any "
"invalid certificate errors in client code. The `authorized` property on "
"the socket of the incoming request will show if the client certificate "
"was valid. The `authorizationError` property will give the reason if the "
"certificate was not valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_client-certificate.md:11
msgid "Client Certificate Authentication"
msgstr ""

